# Thomas Test Suite Project

This is a Thomas test project initialized with `thomas init`.

## Quick Start

The `examples/` folder is ready to run as-is, against a real public API
(`jsonplaceholder.typicode.com`) — no local server, no extra setup, just an
internet connection.

```bash
thomas request --environment examples/config/environments/example.json \
                --folder examples/scenarios \
                --variables examples/config/variables.example.json \
                --title "Thomas Quickstart"
```

`thomas request` prints the path of the execution record it just wrote
(under `executions/`). Use that same path for the next two commands:

```bash
thomas validate --execution executions/<execution-record-from-above>.json \
                 --environment examples/config/environments/example.json

thomas report --execution executions/<execution-record-from-above>.json \
               --environment examples/config/environments/example.json
```

Open the generated `.html` file in `reports/` to see the results.

## Your Own Scenarios

### 1. Configure Environment

Copy the example environment and add your API base URL:

```bash
cp config/environments/example.json.dist config/environments/example.json
# Edit config/environments/example.json and set your api base_url
```

### 2. Add Test Scenarios

Create test scenario files in the `scenarios/` directory:

```bash
cat > scenarios/my_test.json << 'EOF'
{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "feature": "my_feature",
  "scenario_id": "my_scenario",
  "description": "Test my feature",
  "endpoint": {
    "method": "POST",
    "path": "/api/endpoint"
  },
  "api_checks": [
    {
      "id": "status_ok",
      "field": "status_code",
      "operator": "equals",
      "expected_value": 200
    }
  ]
}
EOF
```

### 3. Run Tests

```bash
thomas request \
  --environment config/environments/example.json \
  --folder scenarios \
  --variables config/variables.example.json \
  --title "My Test Run"
```

### 4. Generate Report

```bash
thomas report --execution executions/<execution-record>.json \
               --environment config/environments/example.json
```

## Project Structure

- `scenarios/` — Your test scenarios (JSON files)
- `config/environments/` — Environment configurations (credentials, base URLs)
- `config/variables.example.json` — Shared test variables
- `examples/` — Ready-to-run reference scenarios against a real public API
- `.gitignore` — Recommended ignores (customize as needed)

## Documentation

For more information, see the [Thomas Test Suite documentation](https://github.com/serjupla/the-thomas-test-suite).
